<% title "Join Fuime" %>
<% page_full %>

<%# Fuime: the join link was opened while signed in as somebody else — most
    often the parent who sent it, on the laptop they share.

    This page reveals the redacted address the link was sent to and nothing
    else: not the teen's name, not the parent's, not the venture. The link
    signs its holder in AS THE TEEN, so the one thing this screen must not do
    is offer a way to proceed. %>
<main class="center max-w-xl card mt4 md-p3 mx-auto">
  <h1 class="mt0 border-0 mb-2">This link is for a different account</h1>

  <p class="text-lg mb-3">
    It was sent to <strong><%= @invited_email %></strong>, but you're signed in
    as <strong><%= current_user.email %></strong>.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    Sign out, then open the link again and sign in with the address it was sent to.
  </p>

  <%= button_to "Sign out and open the link again", logout_users_path,
                method: :delete,
                class: "btn bg-accent",
                form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>

  <p class="text-sm muted mt-4 text-center">
    Questions? Contact us at <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %>
  </p>
</main>
